  "published": "2026-11-07T10:26:19.83Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v17.1.1 / v18.1.1: Version lines now follow the Umbraco major (17.x for Umbraco 17, 18.x for Umbraco 18) and each line's Umbraco.Cms.Web.Common dependency is boxed to a single major - [17.0.0, 18.0.0) and [18.0.0, 19.0.0) respectively. Previously a single net10.0 build declared [17.0.0, 19.0.0), which let a host pinned to Umbraco 17 be pulled up to Umbraco 18 whenever another package in the project graph demanded 18. Boxing the range per major prevents that cross-major drift: installing into an Umbraco 17 site always resolves the 17.x line and never forces an 18 upgrade. Umbraco 16 (the old net9.0 target) is no longer supported. No functional, API, UI or database changes - this is a packaging/compatibility change only. v1.0.1: The backoffice package manifest now ships correctly - the project uses the Razor SDK with StaticWebAssetBasePath so umbraco-package.json is packed and discovered under App_Plugins/utpro-geo-location/, and the manifest version stays in sync with the package version. No runtime changes. v1.0.0: Initial release. IP-based geolocation with CDN header detection (Cloudflare, AWS, Azure) and offline MMDB fallback. Country-to-culture mapping, Umbraco middleware integration, and configurable provider chain.",
